a40979bdf4637412872cb1b96","title":"Can universal holographic data of moduli-stabilised AdS4 vacua, especially LVS, make their quantum-gravity consistency accessible through unitarity and crossing constraints on putative three-dimensional CFT duals?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0035"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:db99a42234a324f92a5804c0fc005c5aa231c3ba422234b37feb4ee4e949a9be","title":"After including the finite light throat tower, do the AdS and dS extrema persist, or were they artifacts of an unreliable truncation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:db1da7fc8f9868ed77110bfe577656b9105f361209e522d50ff0ff56dde81c89","title":"Can classical type II compactifications admit de Sitter solutions within a regime of weak string coupling and large internal volume, and can their instability be established within the restricted source ansatz?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:dbb9485a225b2430e8be3ebba03b1ec654b60104333862d9f62631c272b35af4","title":"Must every scalar's self-interactions remain stronger than gravity throughout field space?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0040"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:dbacf0f5c51e0214b74021e77aecf39e77641f8cb4c2282e00a4cb4b74d73101","title":"Can a cancellation in Higgs self-interactions require new physics even when its mass is far below the Planck scale?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0040"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:dbab507f6e4b0cd64a2fa705867b41594df8ffdd70b0230660fd6ffb205f1f28","title":"Does dark energy evolve measurably rather than behave as a cosmological constant? The proposed test measures w(z)=p(z)/ρ(z) and compares it with −1, independently of whether swampland conjectures are correct.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0040"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:db8bb2cf13b3111877f20fe4f456a11c5a3903a033e7041164bf1e4e7f95a1cd","title":"Which dimensions and supersymmetries permit parametrically light massive AdS supergravitons through holographic coupling of two SCFTs, and what microscopic physics explains the effective theory's breakdown as the graviton mass vanishes?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0041"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:dbbdd47aba188f2d225dbb65549f4b971e5bc29bb74e25bcc57120be0957fcf4","title":"Can UV/IR mixing generate a parametrically light scale from ultraviolet dynamics, violating Wilsonian expectations without tuning? The paper tests how general this mechanism is and how it depends on ultraviolet sensitivity.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0045"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:db36478d1a3a272f7cdb491e45e11cf23c95ea6b5f806994aff8aaa933eaf48f","title":"Can a modified expansion law increase Hubble damping without requiring a conventionally flat potential? The imported brane cosmology changes the relation between potential energy and H while retaining the scalar damping equation.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0048"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:db14babc41641f2bc8d3864acfc4ee8bca5483524f9969dd1d9b0f160b4ecf2f","title":"Can global symmetries, broken only by nonperturbative gravity, explain tiny Dirac neutrino masses through symmetry-preserving Planck-suppressed operators and predict axion dark matter or observable neutrino decays?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0050"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:dbf745fbd923e0cc1905372b371feaa5fbb1ad31ef25469c8e837c8b8cb0f240","title":"Can higher-excitation solutions of the semiclassical Wheeler–DeWitt equation enlarge inflaton-displacement uncertainty and relax eternal-inflation conditions, and do nonlinear interactions or entropy favor the lowest excitation?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0055"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:dbbe1d68d9d0e934e701f1458645c55cac842b17864265127fcd2cf7dd197110","title":"Can fermionic strong dynamics jointly produce a composite Higgs, break an enlarged QCD color group, and generate composite axions whose enhanced masses remain compatible with solving strong CP?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0055"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:dbff441194c33c7fa3834fd9a9a9bca18a31e8bb6ae6e6bdd023ddd43298147a","title":"How can an infinitely cyclic model avoid accumulating entropy in each successive cycle? CBE proposes selecting an almost empty causal patch after prolonged accelerated expansion, leaving matter and most entropy outside the contracting subsystem.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0058"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:db8dcbb524b03ac8b235266bce4cb17ebe1de2b2cf02d4671307db6b7a2f66a7","title":"Which hierarchies among axion potential, Standard Model, and instanton couplings are theoretically motivated, experimentally accessible, and obtainable through simple multi-axion mechanisms?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0060"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:dbed9b6879afe9a03c27774aa14c0f3595a9a18d55979fecac48c074509831f2","title":"Can noncatastrophic gravitino production explain dark matter, and can the GSC be related to other proposed quantum-gravity constraints? The paper develops neither an abundance calculation nor an implication involving the GSC.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0063"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:dbae2d3db794789215b94d1b87d3169d3ac3144bb533a2e2fdd0f1034b1eda85","title":"Can S-duality be established geometrically for every tree-level q-map space, combined with known universal isometries, and used to construct finite-volume fibers and explicit twistor lifts?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0071"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:dbd47969c9ec3632bea8101f7ea2f90536dc6fbf15644102a5d268b5019a8c6d","title":"What does the conjectural confinement bound Λc ≳ H imply for holographic theories in de Sitter space, with scalar stabilization and finite-lived extrema?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0075"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:dbdf46851a4b8e153d89239c5ed065066ceece92835042a21422f3ea72454cbc","title":"Can an apparent horizon carry more entropy than any stationary AdS black hole at the same mass in a holographically consistent gravity theory?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0076"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:db1b691d29260356b65c19d4cded4407d96ae2c3bc4dd0cd3143d84a3b0d9ca3","title":"How do framing changes for a fixed plumbing graph affect BPS q-series, and which spectral features dominate their PCA representations? The proposed gap conjecture concerns the relative saliency of early consecutive-exponent ratios.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0088"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:db9a4652c1635bedae9d310e76a97fdbfc7a42c6cf3e9e823706c63d9ea7352b","title":"Does the number of flux-stabilized moduli obey a linear tadpole-charge bound in the deep interior of a non-geometric moduli space, what coefficient is supported, and can supersymmetric Minkowski solutions have every modulus massive within the tadpole budget?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0089"},"indexTempla