gy during this homogeneous decay?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0109"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:dba3143a0d8e08db8b8b1e8de19478e2d37d15123f2c7b5ecab4df462ba6a0af","title":"Can a gravitational description of eternal BTZ reproduce finite-volume unitary relaxation and Poincaré recurrences, rather than indefinite quasinormal decay? Does summing semiclassical topologies suffice, or is a nonperturbative modification of the horizon needed?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0112"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:dbd6e4ec5ece242fe7c477a233e4ac4874631f8e2259729c266574195db515f2","title":"Do the bosonic equations of anomaly-free supergravity satisfy, to all orders in α′, the differential consistency condition required of a candidate heterotic-string effective theory and of equations derivable from a generally covariant action?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0117"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:db02c49ec1a35fbe639f77c65e1f7960cd2b881bec7a1964fda6dc21606ae951","title":"How can exact supersymmetric constraints remain Wilsonian RG invariant when canonically normalized bare fields acquire wavefunction factors? What does the required transformation of the dynamical scale imply for flat-direction potentials and the inverted hierarchy?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0119"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:dba158bc7ce92d15914355d6bcfe1b96cb911572df0271fb4d62ef1a5c2c393d","title":"How can the functional renormalisation group connect microscopic actions to macroscopic quantum physics, and provide evidence for a predictive, non-perturbative UV completion of gravity?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0121"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"}],"relations":[{"id":"source-access:5d6872a510f296c98102a354","source